I ruled on game-sim-1 and committed the change as `70f0bc16`. The ruling is in `/Users/mindlace/Projects/sfhousing/.claude/worktrees/incremental-game/.superpowers/superconductor/incremental-game/rulings/game-sim-1.md`.

**Ruling:** `game-sim` deletes the one component test case that tests the old Remix hand-off to `/sim`. The case is "after Remix, /sim shows the remixed document over the earlier v2 autosave" in `src/routes/s/[id]/page.view.svelte.spec.ts`. `game-sim` changes nothing else in that file, which still belongs to `game-shell`.

- **Why:** `/sim` no longer takes a Remix hand-off, so the case tests behaviour that is gone. Deleting it keeps `game-sim`'s branch passing `npm run test:unit`. Only the e2e remix tests stay red between the two merges, as the spec already said.
- **Merge rule:** `game-sim` and `game-shell` can still run together. `game-shell`'s plan already rewrites the Remix tests in that file, so the two may conflict there. Whichever unit merges second keeps `game-shell`'s Remix tests and no hand-off case.
- **Not changed:**
  - The unused `sfhSimRemix` type in `src/app.d.ts` stays for `closing` to remove.
  - How `game-sim`'s e2e seeds published policies is left to its operator, since the spec doesn't fix a method.

**Files amended:**
- the design doc: the `game-sim` write-set row and a new ordering note for that file
- the `game-sim` spec: its file list and "Existing tests"
- the `game-shell` spec: a line saying no case mounts `/sim` after Remix

No interface row changed. `game-sim` and `game-shell` are both marked as clarifications, so neither branch is cut back. Their build-graph rows need the new file entry.

My commit also includes the uncommitted edits to `ledger.md` that were already in the worktree. I didn't write them; `git add` on the three docs swept them in.
